  "query_preview": "..\nSYNOPTIC SETUP:\nStrong low pressure over south-central Canada will continue moving\naway allowing surface low pressure over the northern Rockies to\novertop the CWA this afternoon. This will allow for decreasing NW\nwinds and decreasing clouds across the eastern zones.\n\nThe next system is dropping into the Pacific NW from the NW. It is\nexpected to continue dropping south and into northern California\nWednesday and Thursday before lifting into the northern Rockies\nlate Thursday or Friday. With dewpoints expected to be in the 50s\nand 60s Friday, showers and thunderstorms can be expected. Models\nare showing the system to cut-off and drift east allowing things\nto gradually dry out Saturday and Saturday night.\n\nRain totals with this system could be close to an inch in some\nplaces in the east with places in the west at or below a quarter\ninch.\n\nEnsembles for next week are showing some drying and slightly\nwarmer temps.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n- Mainly rode with NBM numbers for this forecast package.\n\n- Confidence in rain chances this weekend are moderate. Confidence\n  in rain totals are low. NBM lowered rain totals with this latest\n  run.\n\nTFJ",
